WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.103
-As the Senate impeachment trial
enters its next phase,

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:06.438
the President and his lawyers
have gone from arguing

00:00:06.438 --> 00:00:09.075
that there was no quid pro quo
to arguing that

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.211
the President can do literally
whatever he wants.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.212
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:17.383
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:20.086
Democratic House prosecutors
have laid out a very clear,

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.755
specific, detailed case against
President Trump.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:26.192
He held up hundreds of millions
of dollars in aid to Ukraine

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.528
in order to extort that country
to help him cheat

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:31.464
in the 2020 election by digging
up dirt on Joe Biden.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.767
Congressman Jason Crow,
a combat veteran,

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.735
put it in very simple terms.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:40.406
-We are here for one reason
and one reason only.

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.975
The President
of the United States

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:45.044
withheld foreign aid

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:50.983
that he was happy to give
in the two prior years,

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:53.753
that suddenly we are
to believe something changed,

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.354
the conditions
on the ground changed

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:58.357
and he had an epiphany
about corruption

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:01.193
within a week
of Vice President Biden

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:04.196
announcing his candidacy.

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:05.931
It doesn't make any sense.

00:01:05.931 --> 00:01:08.400
-No, it doesn't, mostly
because Trump isn't capable

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.102
of having an epiphany.

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:14.474
His brain is only capable of
firing one neuron at a time.

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.976
If he ever tried to do
a math problem,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.479
he'd forget to breathe
and pass out.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:22.749
That's why he looks dead into
the camera with that blank stare

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:25.885
like a deer caught
in a nature video.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.854
Not only has Trump never heard
of an epiphany in his life,

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:30.456
if you asked him what
an epiphany was,

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:33.092
he'd probably say,
"The daughter who hates me?"

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.560
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.530
"She's a real piphany."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:41.000
And as the Democratic House
prosecutors have laid out

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.268
their evidence in the Senate
impeachment trial,

00:01:43.268 --> 00:01:46.205
President Trump's defense team
has struggled to respond.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.274
It's getting harder and harder
for Trump to insist that

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.843
the investigation is a so-called
witch hunt.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:54.013
And I mean it's literally
getting physically harder

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.449
for him to say
the words "witch hunt."

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.918
-The American people are
disgusted by

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.387
the Washington Democrat wish --

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.689
And you see it.
You see it.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.825
Seth: "Wish -- what -- what --

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.161
Witch, witch, what?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:11.364
We don't. We don't know
what you said.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.865
Why does he always do that thing

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:15.201
where he just quickly moves on
and pretends he didn't mess up

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.203
instead of just stopping
and correcting himself?

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.838
It's not a slick move, dude.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.473
It makes you sound like a stoner

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.908
with a mouth full
of peanut butter.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:27.146
[ Mumbling ]

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:29.582
Witch, witch, was.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.751
And when he's not complaining
about a witch hunt,

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:32.985
Trump has repeatedly claimed

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:34.787
that Article 2
of the Constitution,

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.056
which outlines
the powers of the presidency,

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.859
allows him to do literally
whatever he wants.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.127
-Article 2 allows me to do
whatever I want.

00:02:42.127 --> 00:02:44.264
Then I have an Article 2,

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:47.099
where I have the right to do
whatever I want as President,

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:49.935
but I don't even
talk about that.

00:02:49.935 --> 00:02:51.971
Nobody ever mentions
Article 2.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.840
It gives me all of these rights

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.610
at a level that nobody
has ever seen before.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.679
-What do you mean nobody
has ever seen before?

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:02.281
Only Trump would think,
"No one ever gets to that part

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:04.584
because it's all the way back
in Article 2."

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:05.851
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:07.487
Of course,
I doubt Trump has ever read

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.389
even one full sentence
of the Constitution.

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:11.090
He probably got three words in
and quit.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.127
"We, the people? I think that
'M' is upside down."

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:15.761
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:20.366
[ Applause ]
Or maybe, maybe it's possible --

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:23.202
it's possible Trump just got
some bad legal advice.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.703
After all, look who's
representing him

00:03:24.703 --> 00:03:25.905
in the impeachment trial.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.607
Here's one of his lawyers,
Pam Bondi,

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.543
the former Attorney General
of Florida trying to claim

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.612
that Joe Biden's son,
Hunter, was corrupt

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.580
and worth investigating,
except she clearly

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.583
could not find her notes
and was lost without them.

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:41.888
-He remained on the board...

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:44.390
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.059
...until...

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:50.329
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.664
...April...

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.332
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:54.600
...of...

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.970
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:02.074
...2019.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:04.043
-Pam Bondi...

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:07.080
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.181
...you...

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:12.885
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.020
[ Bleep ]

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:18.257
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.358
...up.

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:22.861
[ Cheers and applause ]
Where --

00:04:22.861 --> 00:04:24.864
[ Cheering continues ]

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.967
Where does Trump
find these lawyers?

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:30.837
Did he see her on a bus stop
bench ad?

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:34.173
Or just on a bus stop bench?

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.943
She's like a failed game show
contestant whose fallback career

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.377
was defending the President.

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:41.514
Ms. Bondi, who is
Hunter Biden?

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:44.784
-He remained on the board...

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:47.887
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.089
...until...

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.059
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.593
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:57.430
I have not seen
a swing and a miss that bad

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:00.633
since that British lady whiffed
on Greta Thunberg's name.

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.168
-The 2019 book entitled

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:04.137
"No One Is Too Small
to Make a Difference"

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.339
is a collection of speeches
made by

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:08.241
a Swedish climate change
activist.

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:09.742
What's her name?

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:12.011
-Sharon.
-Greta Thunberg.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:17.250
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:21.354
-She looks like a Sharon.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:23.823
But Trump's claim that he can do
whatever he wants

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:26.092
is very much at the core
of Trumpism

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:28.294
and the modern Republican Party.

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.396
And that ethos is very much
on display

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.697
in this impeachment trial.

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:33.465
Republicans have spent
a decade pretending to be

00:05:33.465 --> 00:05:35.567
a principled party based on
limited government

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:37.103
and respect for
the Constitution,

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:39.438
where in reality they never
cared about any of that stuff.

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:41.440
Today's Republican Party is
an authoritarian movement

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.176
led by people who believe
they should have the power

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:45.811
to impose their will
on everyone else.

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:49.315
And Trump perfectly embodies
that authoritarian mindset,

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:51.483
which was on display
in its clearest

00:05:51.483 --> 00:05:53.118
and most obvious form yesterday

00:05:53.118 --> 00:05:54.620
when Trump lawyer
Alan Dershowitz

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.056
made a truly shocking
argument that it doesn't matter

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:59.625
if Trump engaged in
an illegal quid pro quo

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.326
to cheat in the 2020 election,

00:06:01.326 --> 00:06:04.029
because if he was doing
something to help himself

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:07.232
get re-elected, that means
he was also doing it

00:06:07.232 --> 00:06:08.767
in the national interest.

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:11.003
-Every public official
that I know

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:14.940
believes that his election
is in the public interest.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.410
And mostly you're right.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.179
Your election is
in the public interest.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:22.849
And if a president
does something

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:26.118
which he believes will
help him get elected

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:28.420
in the public interest,

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:33.259
that cannot be
the kind of quid pro quo

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:35.494
that results in impeachment.

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:38.063
-That is an absolutely
insane argument

00:06:38.063 --> 00:06:40.099
that is antithetical
to literally everything

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.368
the Founders believed when
they wrote the Constitution.

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:43.869
Think about what he's
saying there.

00:06:43.869 --> 00:06:46.271
He's saying that if you believe
you being president

00:06:46.271 --> 00:06:48.040
is what's best for the country,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.742
then you're allowed to do
whatever you want

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.377
in order to remain president.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:53.079
That's insane.
By that logic,

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.314
Trump could shut down airports
under the pretense

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:57.850
of high winds any time one of
his Democratic challengers

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.286
had a flight, which would affect
everyone but Bernie

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:02.355
who likely has a backup mule.

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:04.123
[ Laughter ]
"Mules are stubborn,

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:06.525
no-nonsense and affordable,
just like me."

00:07:06.525 --> 00:07:07.893
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:10.196
"I will see you in Iowa
in one week."

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:13.699
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:16.702
Now, to give you an idea of how
utterly bankrupt and amoral

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.538
this idea is, let's just
step back and review

00:07:18.538 --> 00:07:20.906
how much the Trump team's
argument has changed

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:22.474
over the last few months.

00:07:22.474 --> 00:07:24.243
Because as you just heard,
one of the President's lawyers

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:27.980
literally just said that he can
commit an illegal quid pro quo

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.682
to cheat in an election
and that's fine.

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:32.585
But, as you'll recall, when
the allegations first emerged,

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:34.920
Trump and his supporters
insisted adamantly

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.923
over and over and over again
that no such quid pro quo

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:39.358
had ever occurred.

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:41.327
-There's no quid pro quo,
no demand,

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:43.261
no pressure, no threat.

00:07:43.261 --> 00:07:44.764
-There's no quid pro quo.

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:46.098
-There was no quid pro quo.

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:47.767
-There is no quid pro quo.

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:49.101
-There is no
quid pro quo.

00:07:49.101 --> 00:07:51.136
-There was no quid pro quo.

00:07:51.136 --> 00:07:53.639
-There was no
quid pro quo.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:55.707
There was no quid pro quo.

00:07:55.707 --> 00:07:57.276
But listen to this.

00:07:57.276 --> 00:08:00.379
There is no pro quo.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:02.180
-That's right it.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:04.050
There was no pro quo.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.852
I guess we can't expect the
President of the United States

00:08:06.852 --> 00:08:10.022
to remember that many
one-syllable words.

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:12.124
When Eric and Don Jr. were
growing up, he probably

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:14.460
read them a book called
"The Cat in The."

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:17.663
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:20.232
"No pro quo" sounds like
a fake phrase a New Yorker

00:08:20.232 --> 00:08:22.334
would say to a tourist
in Times Square

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:24.670
to avoid talking to them.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.139
"Excuse me, can you tell us
where the M&amp;M Store is?"

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:28.941
"Scusi, no pro quo."

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:32.010
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.645
So that was their argument
at the start.

00:08:33.645 --> 00:08:36.815
Fast-forward to Tuesday amid
the Senate impeachment trial

00:08:36.815 --> 00:08:39.418
when Senator Ted Cruz
took a rehearsal break

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:41.520
from his
one-man Unabomber musical

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.723
to argue that
it doesn't matter

00:08:43.723 --> 00:08:45.224
if there was a quid pro quo.

00:08:45.224 --> 00:08:47.926
-The Constitution requires
high crimes or misdemeanors.

00:08:47.926 --> 00:08:49.695
That the test for impeachment,

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:53.098
it's treason, bribery, or other
high crimes and misdemeanors.

00:08:53.098 --> 00:08:55.167
And the House Democrats,
they haven't alleged

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:56.902
any crime whatsoever.

00:08:56.902 --> 00:08:59.605
One point that explains why
the President is innocent

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:02.675
and he should be acquitted
and why he will be acquitted.

00:09:02.675 --> 00:09:05.844
Quid pro quo doesn't matter.
It's a red herring.

00:09:05.844 --> 00:09:08.781
It doesn't matter if there was
a quid pro quo or not.

00:09:08.781 --> 00:09:11.350
-Oh, now it doesn't matter?

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:13.719
You guys have spent
the last four months insisting

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:15.020
it didn't happen.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:16.722
When you suddenly change
your argument like that,

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:18.791
it makes it obvious
it did happen.

00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:20.626
If you worked at Dunkin' Donuts
and your boss said to you,

00:09:20.626 --> 00:09:23.329
"Hey, Brad, did you stick your
[bleep] through the crullers?"

00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:25.264
and you said,
"Of course not,"

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:26.965
and then he asked you again,
and you said,

00:09:26.965 --> 00:09:29.568
"It doesn't matter, crullers
taste like [bleep] anyway!"

00:09:29.568 --> 00:09:31.904
[ Laughter ]
Then, yeah,

00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:34.807
you stuck your [bleep]
through all the crullers.

00:09:34.807 --> 00:09:37.276
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:37.276 --> 00:09:39.945
In fact, Ted Cruz himself,

00:09:39.945 --> 00:09:43.516
he once argued there was
definitely no quid pro quo.

00:09:43.516 --> 00:09:45.818
-A lot of what the Democrats
had been raising,

00:09:45.818 --> 00:09:48.721
alleging an illegal
quid pro quo was not,

00:09:48.721 --> 00:09:50.856
in fact, backed up
by the transcript.

00:09:50.856 --> 00:09:52.224
-First of all, it wasn't
a transcript.

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:54.493
The transcript is still in some
secret server

00:09:54.493 --> 00:09:56.528
with a ton of what I'm sure
is other incriminating material.

00:09:56.528 --> 00:09:58.496
And second of all,
even the readout

00:09:58.496 --> 00:10:00.532
the White House released backed
up the quid pro quo.

00:10:00.532 --> 00:10:03.035
When you offer someone something
of value, and then literally

00:10:03.035 --> 00:10:05.270
in the next breath say,
"I would like you to do us

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:07.573
a favor though," as Trump did
on his phone call

00:10:07.573 --> 00:10:08.908
with the President of Ukraine,

00:10:08.908 --> 00:10:11.410
that is the literal definition
of a quid pro quo.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:14.346
And if that person
turns it down,

00:10:14.346 --> 00:10:16.448
the only polite thing to
say is...

00:10:16.448 --> 00:10:19.718
-No pro quo.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:19.718 --> 00:10:21.887
-These guys can't keep
their talking points straight

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:23.756
because they don't have
a coherent defense.

00:10:23.756 --> 00:10:25.457
Just watch this awkward moment

00:10:25.457 --> 00:10:27.993
from Sean Hannity's
Fox News show where he tried

00:10:27.993 --> 00:10:30.762
to tick through four supposed
facts that explain

00:10:30.762 --> 00:10:32.531
why Trump is definitely
innocent,

00:10:32.531 --> 00:10:34.934
and then tossed to GOP
Congressman Jim Jordan

00:10:34.934 --> 00:10:37.102
to explain the fourth fact,

00:10:37.102 --> 00:10:38.938
but Jordan seemed
to have no idea

00:10:38.938 --> 00:10:40.272
what he was supposed to say.

00:10:40.272 --> 00:10:43.542
-Jim Jordan, four facts
never change,

00:10:43.542 --> 00:10:46.645
and why is that relevant
again tonight?

00:10:46.645 --> 00:10:49.849
Because let's say John Bolton
said the President vented.

00:10:49.849 --> 00:10:53.051
President said, "Ah, I --
they better do this

00:10:53.051 --> 00:10:54.620
or they're not
getting any money."

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:58.057
The fourth fact is?

00:10:58.057 --> 00:11:00.259
[ Laughter ]

00:11:00.259 --> 00:11:03.862
Of your facts, the fourth fact
is it doesn't matter, does it?

00:11:03.862 --> 00:11:05.364
'Cause he didn't do it.

00:11:05.364 --> 00:11:08.300
-Ha, ha.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.468
[ Chuckles ]

00:11:09.468 --> 00:11:11.436
[ Laughter ]

00:11:11.436 --> 00:11:13.104
That was the equivalent
of watching someone

00:11:13.104 --> 00:11:15.674
pass a basketball to a teammate
who's not looking

00:11:15.674 --> 00:11:18.643
and have it bounce
right off their face.

00:11:18.643 --> 00:11:21.780
Even Pam Bondi was like,
"Get it together, guys."

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:22.981
[ Laughter ]

00:11:22.981 --> 00:11:24.649
Trump's lawyers and allies

00:11:24.649 --> 00:11:26.885
can't keep their talking points
straight because it's all B.S.

00:11:26.885 --> 00:11:28.787
They're making up stuff
off the top of their heads

00:11:28.787 --> 00:11:30.922
to mask the only real argument
they actually have,

00:11:30.922 --> 00:11:32.658
which is this -- they want to
keep Trump in office,

00:11:32.658 --> 00:11:34.192
and in order to do that,
they have to agree

00:11:34.192 --> 00:11:35.360
he's above the law.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:36.561
They've said as much

00:11:36.561 --> 00:11:37.897
throughout
this impeachment trial.

00:11:37.897 --> 00:11:39.464
The Republican Party is an
authoritarian movement

00:11:39.464 --> 00:11:41.333
beholden to their
cult-like leader.

00:11:41.333 --> 00:11:43.068
That's been clear
since the moment

00:11:43.068 --> 00:11:44.637
Trump announced his candidacy.

00:11:44.637 --> 00:11:47.105
But it's been especially obvious
since at least...

00:11:47.105 --> 00:11:49.741
-April...
[ Laughter ]

00:11:49.741 --> 00:11:50.976
...of...

00:11:50.976 --> 00:11:54.312
[ Applause ]

00:11:54.312 --> 00:11:56.114
...2019.

00:11:56.114 --> 00:11:58.417
-Oh, Pam!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:58.417 --> 00:12:00.018
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:00.018 --> 00:12:03.222
[ Cheers and applause ]

